# SCRIMP v1.3.0 Docker: STRICT ALLOWLIST, not a blacklist.
# Docker sends only these source files to the builder. Untracked/user
# simulation data, snapshots, meshes, logs, screenshots, PDFs, videos,
# generated outputs, and arbitrarily named local directories are excluded
# regardless of their location in the repository.
#
# Important: each ancestor directory of an exception must be unignored.
# "docker/Dockerfile" is also transferred by Docker even if ignored, but
# we include it explicitly to make this manifest self-documenting.
**

# Installation metadata / package license
!setup.py
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# Docker definition and dependency lock input
!docker/
!docker/Dockerfile
!docker/environment.yml

# Core SCRIMP Python package, including GUI and utils modules
!scrimp/
!scrimp/*.py
!scrimp/GUI/
!scrimp/GUI/*.py
!scrimp/utils/
!scrimp/utils/*.py

# Executable examples only (exclude Jupyter notebooks, results, data)
!examples/
!examples/*.py
!examples/published/
!examples/published/*/
!examples/published/*/*.py

# Python tests and diagnostic/sandbox source scripts only;
# NEVER include sandbox outputs, numerical dumps, movies or figures.
!tests/
!tests/*.py
!tests/perf/
!tests/perf/*.py
!sandbox/
!sandbox/*.py
!sandbox/*.sh

# Release/build helpers and approved GetFEM patches only
!scripts/
!scripts/*.sh
!scripts/*.py
!scripts/patches/
!scripts/patches/getfem-5.5/
!scripts/patches/getfem-5.5/*.patch
